==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{der|es|la|cervesia}}, variant of {{m|la|cervisia}} (compare {{cog|an|zerbeza}}, {{cog|ca|cervesa}}, {{cog|gl|cervexa}}, {{cog|pt|cerveja}}), perhaps related to {{m|la|cremor||juice, thick [[broth]]}}, but likely from {{der|es|cel-gau|*kerβ ̃-}}, e-vocalism of {{etyl|cel-pro|es}} {{m|cel-pro|*kormi||beer}}, from {{der|es|ine-pro|*ḱr̥h₃m-||soup}}. Compare Welsh [[cwrw]].

